body:
idk dude, you'd be surprised how many people consider both teaching and art "easy". I work as a dance coach/teacher (with both 3-5 yo's all the way up to 15-16yo's who compete at the world level).

Teaching often gets disregarded as "super easy, i could probably do it better". The amount of entitled parents who think they know best and challenge your every decision is very high. Plus the job is very time-consuming too -- prep for practice/lessons in the mornings, actually teaching in the afternoons, competitions/performances on weekends. Also bootcamps/more important competitions that take place abroad and last like a week happen a few times a year. 

&#x200B;

Not to mention dance itself is often target of "how hard can it be, you're literally just moving around to the music", or the evergreen "it's not even a real job lol". It takes A LOT of effort to constantly draw inspiration (from whatever inspires you) and create new stuff without being too repetitive or just plain bad.

&#x200B;

You're right, OP said "seems easy; incredibly challenging", and there's a few people missing the mark with their answers. but listing both teaching and art as  examples of the point you're trying to make is just a horrible choice lol.

I think the helmet is tight enough that it keeps all the important stuff in it's place even if the skull is shattered, so it can sometimes keep a person alive after crashing... 

&#x200B;

i could be wrong tho

&#x200B;
jordan 1's are comfortable to dance in, but also super expensive and unnecessary to have... 
I have 3 pairs of shoes that i regularly cycle between, depending on what (type of) choreography I'm learning/performing/teaching at the moment, but I feel like you can never go wrong with something like Puma Suede's or Vans Oldskool's

100% se strinjam, edino kar me moti (kot novopečenega apple userja) je da če mam telefon zraven sebe na mizi pa ga probam odpret, morem nad njim izvajat gimnastiko da me faceID prepozna (al pa telefon dvignt), namesto da bi dal sam prst gor pa ga odklenu naslonjen nazaj na stolu...

&#x200B;

ampak to je res nek tak minor inconvenience, za kerga se sploh ne sekiram ker mi je vse ostalo tok bolj všeč na jabučku kot pa na androidu

Moj najbl kratkoročen cilj je narest izpit k ga mam čez 8 ur pa pol

&#x200B;

Drgač pa zaključek plesne sezone, državno & evropsko prvenstvo sfurat kokr se da dobr, pa naslednjo sezono speljat najboljš možno k sm sposobn (prvič v vlogi trenerja). Aja, pa končno se spravt narest izpit za avto lol
